{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-311977",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=22$ and $x=25$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(22)=f(25)=7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=22$ and $x=25.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{22+25}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{47}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
